cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived software release and the associated manuscript."

title: "Reproducibility Software for Numerical Certification and Approximation Benchmarking of an Experimentally Anchored Soft-Core Atom-Ion Radial Hamiltonian"

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Abu Ayyash"
    given-names: "Mohammad"
    affiliation: "Al-Quds University"

version: "1.0.2"
date-released: 2026-08-02

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  Reproducibility source code, tests, and execution metadata supporting
  numerical certification and fixed-operator approximation benchmarking
  of an experimentally anchored effective soft-core atom-ion radial
  Hamiltonian. The software includes fourth-order finite-difference
  calculations, continuum extrapolation, independent Numerov validation,
  WKB quantization, variational calculations, perturbative-breakdown
  diagnostics, non-perturbative harmonic-oscillator-basis diagonalization,
  regulator-dependence analysis, angular-sector diagnostics, and
  zero-energy boundary calculations. The numerical precision reported by
  the software characterizes the selected frozen operator and must not be
  interpreted as comparable physical accuracy for the complete Paul-trap
  system or its dynamical formation process.

keywords:
  - atom-ion
  - effective Hamiltonian
  - soft-core potential
  - radial Hamiltonian
  - numerical benchmark
  - finite-difference method
  - continuum extrapolation
  - Numerov method
  - WKB quantization
  - variational method
  - perturbation theory
  - harmonic-oscillator basis
  - regulator dependence
  - reproducible research

repository-code: "https://github.com/mohammadayyash3-star/soft-core-atom-ion-radial-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/mohammadayyash3-star/soft-core-atom-ion-radial-benchmark"